# SRT.Core.RuntimeSettings (Cursor rule template)

This file is an **install template**. Copy it to the consumer project’s `.cursor/rules/` and keep the package-prefixed filename:

`SRT.Core.RuntimeSettings.CURSOR_RULE.mdc`

## Mandatory

Before using or modifying this package, follow:

- `docs/SRT.Core.RuntimeSettings.AI_RULES.md` (canonical)
- `docs/SRT.Core.RuntimeSettings.API_REFERENCE.md`
- `docs/SRT.Core.RuntimeSettings.COOKBOOK.md` when wiring a service

## Working rule

Read docs first. Do not invent APIs. If ambiguous, inspect the code and update the docs.

## Hard constraints (summary)

- Every registered key has an initial value in appsettings
- Read a registered key from `IOptionsMonitor` or `IRuntimeSettings` each time, unless `requiresRestart: true`
- Do not register passwords, tokens, or connection strings
- Call `SRT_AddRuntimeSettings` from the service, not from a plugin, so the source exists before the service reads configuration
- Do not call `SRT_AddGeneralConfig` for `RuntimeSettingsDbContext` yourself
